  "datasheet": "https://docs.arduino.cc/resources/datasheets/A000066-datasheet.pdf",
  "verified": true,
  "summary": "The classic 5 V Arduino: ATmega328P at 16 MHz, 14 digital I/O (6 PWM), 6 analog inputs, ATmega16U2 USB-serial bridge.",
  "warnings": [
    {
      "level": "info",
      "text": "All I/O on this board is native 5 V logic: the ATmega328P runs from 5 V, so its pins output 5 V and accept 0 to 5 V (absolute max VCC + 0.5 V). They are not \"5 V tolerant\" pins, they simply are 5 V pins. Connecting a 3.3 V-only device directly to an output pin can damage it; use a level shifter."
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "text": "Pins 0 (RX) and 1 (TX) are shared with the USB-serial chip. Anything connected to them can block sketch uploads and Serial Monitor; disconnect it while uploading.",
      "pins": [
        "JD1-1",
        "JD1-2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "text": "A4 and A5 are the I2C pins SDA and SCL. The SDA/SCL pins next to AREF are the same two signals, so I2C uses up A4 and A5.",
      "pins": [
        "JA-5",
        "JA-6",
        "JD2-9",
        "JD2-10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "text": "Hardware SPI is on 10 (SS), 11 (MOSI), 12 (MISO) and 13 (SCK), and also on the 6-pin ICSP header.",
      "pins": [
        "JD2-3",
        "JD2-4",
        "JD2-5",
        "JD2-6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "text": "Only pins 2 and 3 have external interrupts (INT0/INT1) for attachInterrupt(). Every I/O pin also has a pin-change interrupt (PCINT), which needs direct register code or a library.",
      "pins": [
        "JD1-3",
        "JD1-4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "text": "Current limits: the ATmega328P absolute maximum is 40 mA DC per I/O pin and 200 mA through the VCC and GND pins (Microchip DS40002061B, Absolute Maximum Ratings). The datasheet specifies output levels only up to its 20 mA test condition, and Arduino's official pinout gives 20 mA as the maximum per I/O pin, so design for 20 mA or less per pin. The datasheet also limits the summed current of each port group (see its DC characteristics notes)."
    }
  ],
